{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/SecretsAndTokens","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Secrets and Tokens","modules":[{"name":"LoveLetterCore"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Transports","anchor":"Transports","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/CustomTransports","doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackTransport","doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/GitHubDirectTransport","doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/RelayTransport"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/GitHubDirectTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" requires a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter to POST to GitHub Issues. Wherever that token lives — embedded constant, obfuscated blob, fetched at runtime — the threat model is the same: "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"anyone with the binary can recover the token","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Disassembly, runtime memory dump, or a hooked HTTPS proxy will eventually surface it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK does not pretend otherwise. It exposes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token: String"},{"type":"text","text":" directly and lets you decide the trade-off:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Approach"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Effort","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Resists casual extraction","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Resists determined extraction"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plaintext constant"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"trivial","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"XOR \/ obfuscated blob decoded at runtime"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"small"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Token fetched from your server at app start"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"medium","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"no (once fetched, lives in memory)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Server-side relay holds the token"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"medium-high","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the last row genuinely contains the blast radius. The first three raise the bar; an attacker who actually wants the token will still get it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Acceptable use of an embedded token","anchor":"Acceptable-use-of-an-embedded-token","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A PAT inside the binary is reasonable when:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The repo is a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"write-only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" feedback inbox and the worst-case abuse is spam issues you can delete."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can rotate the PAT quickly if abuse occurs (and have monitoring to notice)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The PAT’s scope is the minimum that lets it open issues — typically ","type":"text"},{"code":"public_repo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"repo"},{"type":"text","text":" for a private repo, nothing more."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You’re comfortable with someone using the same endpoint to spam your inbox.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If any of these stop being true, move to a relay.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Moving to a relay","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Moving-to-a-relay"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cleanest mitigation is to keep the credential on a server you control and expose a thin HTTPS endpoint. The SDK ships a ready-made "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/RelayTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" for exactly this — point it at your relay’s URL and your app never sees a GitHub token:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let transport = RelayTransport(","    endpoint: URL(string: \"https:\/\/your-relay.example.com\/api\/feedback\")!,","    captchaTokenProvider: { await captcha.freshToken() }  \/\/ optional, fetched per submit",")","let feedback = FeedbackClient(appName: \"AcmeApp\", transport: transport)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/RelayTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is wire-compatible with the same relays the Love Letter Web and Android SDKs target. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/CustomTransports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if you need to write your own transport for a different backend."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once the relay holds the token, you also get:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rate-limiting per device \/ IP without burning GitHub’s API quota."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Spam filters before they reach your repo.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional attachments (screenshots, logs) via your own CDN — the GitHub REST API doesn’t accept binary uploads, but your server can mirror to one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Schema evolution without shipping a new app version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Dont-store-tokens-in-your-repo","text":"Don’t store tokens in your repo"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Even if you’re embedding a PAT in the binary, the source should never have it in plaintext. Common pattern:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep the obfuscated\/encoded form in source."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode it at runtime just before constructing the transport.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Restrict the PAT scope to issues-write only.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Have a documented rotation procedure."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Topics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/GitHubDirectTransport","doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/RelayTransport","doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/CustomTransports"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/secretsandtokens"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Shipping a GitHub Personal Access Token inside an app binary is a known trade-off. Here’s how the SDK handles it honestly.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore/FeedbackReport":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackReport","title":"FeedbackReport","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FeedbackReport"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FeedbackReport","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A single user-supplied feedback submission.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/feedbackreport","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore":{"url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Submit feedback from any Apple platform to a GitHub repository in the exact body format the Love Letter inbox parses."}],"title":"LoveLetterCore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore/CustomTransports":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/CustomTransports","kind":"article","title":"Custom Transports","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/customtransports","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Replace "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/GitHubDirectTransport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with a relay server, a mock, or any other backend by conforming to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackTransport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore/FeedbackTransport":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FeedbackTransport"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackReport","isActive":true},{"text":" gets delivered.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FeedbackTransport"}],"title":"FeedbackTransport","url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/feedbacktransport","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackTransport"},"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore/RelayTransport":{"url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/relaytransport","title":"RelayTransport","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that posts reports to an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"adopter-operated relay"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead of to GitHub directly."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/RelayTransport","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RelayTransport","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RelayTransport","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LoveLetterCore/documentation/LoveLetterCore/GitHubDirectTransport":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/GitHubDirectTransport","title":"GitHubDirectTransport","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GitHubDirectTransport","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GitHubDirectTransport","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoveLetterCore\/documentation\/LoveLetterCore\/FeedbackTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that posts reports directly to the GitHub Issues"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"REST API."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/lovelettercore\/githubdirecttransport","kind":"symbol"}}}